From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:53:27 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] unix/unix_mphal: a dupterm stream may detach itself while the
 REPL waits.

mp_hal_stdin_rx_chr() checked dupterm slot 0 once and then called
call_dupterm_read(0) for as long as the stream's read() returned None.
read() runs Python, and that code, or a timer or scheduled callback that
runs during it, can take the stream off with os.dupterm(None, 0). The
next call then looked up read() on a NULL object and the process died
with SIGSEGV. A desktop app that mirrors the REPL through dupterm and
detaches it when it closes does exactly this.

call_dupterm_read() now returns -1 for an empty slot, so the REPL goes
back to reading stdin as soon as the stream is gone.

It also returned -2 for a read() of None, and -1 for an empty read, from
inside its nlr_push() without popping it. The handler it left on top of
the stack pointed into a frame that had returned, so the next exception
with no newer handler, such as one raised and caught in the function
that called input(), jumped there instead of to its own handler. Both
paths now pop it first.
---
 ports/unix/unix_mphal.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ports/unix/unix_mphal.c b/ports/unix/unix_mphal.c
index d04e0b96e..196b20b99 100644
--- a/ports/unix/unix_mphal.c
+++ b/ports/unix/unix_mphal.c
@@ -122,7 +122,14 @@ void mp_hal_stdio_mode_orig(void) {
 #endif
 
 #if MICROPY_PY_OS_DUPTERM
+// Read one character from the stream in dupterm slot idx. Returns the
+// character, -2 if the stream has none yet, or -1 if the slot is empty, the
+// stream has ended or it raised. The slot is checked on every call because
+// the stream's read() can run anything, including code that detaches it.
 static int call_dupterm_read(size_t idx) {
+    if (MP_STATE_VM(dupterm_objs[idx]) == MP_OBJ_NULL) {
+        return -1;
+    }
     nlr_buf_t nlr;
     if (nlr_push(&nlr) == 0) {
         mp_obj_t read_m[3];
@@ -130,6 +137,7 @@ static int call_dupterm_read(size_t idx) {
         read_m[2] = MP_OBJ_NEW_SMALL_INT(1);
         mp_obj_t res = mp_call_method_n_kw(1, 0, read_m);
         if (res == mp_const_none) {
+            nlr_pop();
             return -2;
         }
         mp_buffer_info_t bufinfo;
@@ -137,6 +145,7 @@ static int call_dupterm_read(size_t idx) {
         if (bufinfo.len == 0) {
             mp_printf(&mp_plat_print, "dupterm: EOF received, deactivating\n");
             MP_STATE_VM(dupterm_objs[idx]) = MP_OBJ_NULL;
+            nlr_pop();
             return -1;
         }
         nlr_pop();
